  "goodToKnow": "Stutzig is used almost only in stutzig werden (to become suspicious, start to wonder) and jemanden stutzig machen: Sein Schweigen machte sie stutzig. It comes from stutzen, to stop short in surprise (and also to trim a hedge or tail). Synonyms: misstrauisch, skeptisch, argwöhnisch. Don't confuse it with stottern (to stutter)."
